  "findings": [
    "Initial frozen API RED0/1 proves the new per-path owner consumer is unavailable after a genuine saved Git fixture shows the legacy global owner candidate despite an explicit empty-owner rule. It is not a compiler failure; all source/log/hash evidence is retained.",
    "Initial implementation passes the first new contract plus all8 existing area tests, with unchanged inputs. Final ten contracts and three included library pattern/parser tests then pass on the final frozen source; attempts are nonadditive.",
    "Legacy owner_rules parser body remains LF-normalized byte-identical to parentbf648cb. Existing report owner suggestions and replay IDs are not migrated. A separate captured per-path interpretation preserves the complete impactAreas parent and adds exact full-line/owner-token byte evidence, all supported matching-rule positions, base/head qualification and explicit empty-owner winners.",
    "Internal areas::derive_with retains the checked read transaction and validated base/head Snapshot objects while new rule reads/rendering occur. Public area derivation uses an identity callback; existing area and workflow regressions pass without changing their source/evidence contracts.",
    "First captured .github/CODEOWNERS, CODEOWNERS or docs/CODEOWNERS selection lists uncaptured higher-precedence paths; captured-manifest absence does not prove repository absence. Unsupported active rules make winners indeterminate while supported matches remain visible. No missing capability is returned as empty complete ownership.",
    "The finite independent pattern policy, case sensitivity, Unicode scalar question-mark, recursive directory/literal terminals, nonrecursive slashful wildcard terminal, whole-component double-star and unsupported syntax are documented explicitly. Public GitHub documentation informs facts; neither upstream parser equivalence nor actual user/team membership, permissions, reviews, ownership or merge safety is established.",
    "All10 actual saved-Git/CLI contracts pass: explicit empty rules/quotes, same-owner distinct lines/token ranges, base/head and live-source isolation, unsupported candidates, captured-path precedence, exact independent quotas and output, SQL/caller transaction/cancellation/deadline, tampered CAS refusal, offline PATH/output/source-flag admission and malformed options/no initialization. Three pure library cases additionally check pattern/Unicode/CRLF/token behavior.",
    "Final scoped native results include10 new contracts,432 library tests/7 unchanged ignored gates,8 existing area tests and17 existing Git workflow tests. All-target Clippy, format,17 Python tests,typecheck andTypeScript260/3skip pass with frozen inputs. This does not rerun the whole native suite or erase earlier OS1314 Windows security-fixture failures. Hard maxima are not claimed as fully populated maximum-size qualification.",
    "Wider ownership/semantic/compiler interpretations, pushed-ref freshness, full upstream/R1-R9/platform acceptance, main merge and release remain open. The new command starts no Git/provider/network/model, reads no current source fallback and publishes no Store/source/artifact/latest state."
  ],
